    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cbc74637",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: years_ago_slaves_would_be_used_for_farming; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a historical illustration of enslaved people being forced to work under the supervision of a white overseer, overlaid with the text 'years ago slaves would be used for farming.' The overall intent is to evoke a hateful and dehumanizing portrayal of Black people by reifying the historical trauma of slavery and reducing their humanity to a labor-based stereotype. The visual of enslaved individuals being physically restrained and controlled by a white figure, combined with the text, serves to reinforce racist tropes by implicitly suggesting that Black people are inherently suited only for manual labor and are historically and biologically inferior. This is a harmful and hateful representation that perpetuates anti-Black racism by using historical imagery to justify present-day racial hierarchies and stereotypes. The meme does not merely inform but seeks to normalize and legitimize the dehumanization of Black people through the lens of historical oppression.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6a2a185d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
